{
  "version": 1,
  "generator": "tests/story_bench.c (make story)",
  "policy": "A pilot who reads the panel, not the code: holds Burn toward the marker until the brake-distance readout reaches the distance left (6 % short to 14 % past it) or, while Oren's echo is on, until he calls 'turn now'; keeps the thumb on 0-2 frames too long, coasts 0-5 frames, then holds Brake to rest and plans a fresh approach from where it stopped. Waiting for the tanker, it brakes until the speed reads below 0.004-0.02 c and cuts the engine. It does not smooth the wobbling readout. Its hand comes from the run's own stirred seed, re-drawn per leg. Choices follow the path field.",
  "crisis": "the tank gauge in the red (below 1.2) at any moment in the leg, or a failure (a failure counts as a crisis)",
  "failure": "the tank ran dry and a drone or Kestrel's tug had to come, the rocket flew 0.8 ly past the marker or took 9 ship years over one leg, or the tanker's clamp glanced off",
  "segments": ["Earth to the Gate", "out to the Depot", "through the dust to Kestrel", "back to the Depot", "the last leg home"],
  "note": "16 seeds x 12 runs; every run has its own stirred seed; the path comes from the run number.",
